        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: বানানো",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বানানো — bānāno — \"to make\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বানানো (bānāno) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from vanati, \"desires, makes ready\" (CDIAL 11260). Bānāno is the causing form of banā, a verb CDIAL glosses \"to agree, do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
